+# Menu page swipes and slides (2026-10-04)
+
+Requirements R01/V03/V04/V05/Q01. Owner requests swipes between Race, Create and Garage on content without an existing swipe interaction, preserving the Race track carousel, and phone deployment. Follow-ups request a sliding page effect and a fixed top navigation bar with only content underneath sliding. The fixed-header correction supersedes the original whole-page motion.
+
+## Behavior and changed files
+
+- `game/ui/menu_page_swipe.gd` (and `.uid`): touch recognition owns a gesture according to its starting position. Horizontal intent claims after 16 logical units; release needs 72 units and a 1.5 horizontal/vertical ratio. Short, vertical, canceled and two-finger gestures do not navigate. Ordinary button taps still activate; a swipe starting on a button never fires its action. Native scrolling, text entry, ranges/sliders, popup selectors and press-action controls retain their input. Visible drawers/dialogs block page gestures.
+- `game/core/app.gd`: swiping left advances Race -> Create -> Garage; right reverses, with no wrapping. Create means the biome/draft menus. Reopening creation choices preserves the current document. The editor canvas retains its existing pan/edit gestures. Menu changes between these tabs use a 280 ms horizontal cubic ease-out. The logo, tabs, account and Settings stay fixed; both outgoing and incoming content/scenery slide in a viewport clipped below the header. Full-screen scenic framing is retained inside that clip. Outgoing content ignores GUI input and stops processing; completion, rapid replacement, leaving the tab group and starting a race dispose it. Page gestures are blocked during the slide, when carousel rectangles are moving, then restored at completion. The existing track-selection slide is independent. Same-tab refreshes are immediate.
+- `game/tests/test_menu_page_swipe.gd` (and `.uid`): real viewport-dispatched touches at 1280x720 and 960x540 cover both directions, boundaries, draft preservation, cancellation, multitouch, button taps, carousel scrolling/edge ownership, leaving the carousel, dialogs, editor panning, animation progress/disposal and rapid replacement.
+- This document, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md`, `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md`, and the evidence directory record the slice. No simulation/rules/schema changes.
+
+## Actual verification
+
+All engine commands use `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1` and the pinned Godot `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf` with matching Android templates.
+
+| Command suffix | Actual outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| `-Action Doctor` | DN2103 attached and authorized. |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_menu_page_swipe.gd -Graphical` | Final 68 checks, zero failures; ten desktop/compact screenshots saved. Previous gesture-only runs passed 44, initial slide checks passed 62. |
+| `-Action TestApp` | 96 checks, zero failures, before and after slides. |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_script_parse.gd` | Final 270 scripts, zero failures. |
+| `-Action DeployAndroid -QuickValidation` | All three exports passed import/startup, driving 72, catalog 21 and menu presentation 48 checks, export/install/cold launch. Final guarded-slide APK installed successfully and cold-launched (789 ms). |
+| `git diff --check -- game/core/app.gd` | Passed; existing CRLF normalization notice only. |
+
+Initial direct script invocation was blocked by the local execution policy; explicit `-ExecutionPolicy Bypass` resolves it. Sandbox-only Godot log writes and adb home-directory access failed; authorized tool execution with the required local-directory access succeeded. The first drawer fixture failed because the drawer was still hidden after `_ready`; the test now opens it with its normal `open_for` API. No invariant was weakened. Focused deployment driving checks report three existing ObjectDB shutdown instance leaks. Android export reports build-tools fallback to 35.0.1.
+
+Initial physical-phone testing caught a second swipe during an arrival animation being classified against moving carousel bounds. The final guard and three new checks per size repair this. Phone `screenrecord` is unavailable (`inaccessible or not found`); attempted video capture produced no file. Desktop and actual phone screenshots retain motion evidence instead. No video pass is claimed.
+
+Evidence: [forward slide](evidence/page-swipes-2026-10-04/slide-forward-960x540.png), [reverse slide](evidence/page-swipes-2026-10-04/slide-reverse-960x540.png), [Create](evidence/page-swipes-2026-10-04/create-960x540.png), [carousel](evidence/page-swipes-2026-10-04/race-carousel-960x540.png). Desktop gallery data is an isolated synthetic fixture; no real ratings or completed races are claimed.
+
+Final DN2103 device verification uses `adb shell input swipe` at physical landscape 2400x1080: static-content left/right page gestures, a swipe inside the carousel and a carousel-area swipe immediately after the return-to-Race slide. Final carousel and rapid-swipe screenshots both retain Race. These are actual device checks with adb-generated touches; human finger/feel acceptance is still outstanding. Guest play is left open, with no diagnostic markers installed. Saved [phone forward frame](evidence/page-swipes-2026-10-04/phone-slide-forward.png), [phone carousel protection](evidence/page-swipes-2026-10-04/phone-carousel-protected.png) and [rapid-swipe result](evidence/page-swipes-2026-10-04/phone-fast-swipes.png). The phone has no reachable backend at cold launch; Guest works with cached track metadata. This task does not start or deploy services.
+
+Final logs: gesture `TestScript-18244`, parser `TestScript-16032`, app `TestApp-12124` and deploy `DeployAndroid-28360` under `build/logs`. Focused test/install/launch logs are copied into the evidence directory. APK: `build/android/circuit01-debug.apk`.
+
+Full Validate/replay regression, gameplay driving, sustained device performance and other-device acceptance were not performed for this UI-only task. Owner finger-gesture/animation feel remains an acceptance check. Existing unrelated workspace edits are preserved, and the debug APK includes the current workspace. A scoped Git patch is retained with the evidence instead of committing the mixed workspace.
+
+## Fixed top navigation correction (2026-10-04)
+
+Owner explicitly requires the top bar to remain fixed. `game/core/app.gd` now creates a clipped `MenuContentViewport` below `MenuHeader` and retains only the outgoing content subtree. It moves scenic layers into that body while preserving their original full-screen coordinates. The fixed shell updates the active tab immediately. The existing 280 ms direction/easing, gesture guard, modal/scroll exclusions, draft preservation and cleanup remain.
+
+`game/tests/test_menu_page_swipe.gd` now verifies the full header and Create-tab rectangles remain unchanged during forward and reverse slides, with content clipped below them. Final graphical suite: **76 checks, zero failures**, at 1280x720 and 960x540. Final `TestApp`: **96 checks, zero failures**; parser: **272 scripts, zero failures**; targeted whitespace check passes. Actual commands use the same `scripts/dev.ps1` invocations above. Logs: `TestScript-18468`, `TestApp-21992`, `TestScript-20600`. An initial run failed on a concurrent `RaceModeRail` class-cache miss; pinned `Import` succeeded and unchanged rerun passed. Concurrent rivalry files are outside this correction.
+
+New evidence is under `docs/evidence/fixed-menu-navigation-2026-10-04/`; inspected [forward frame](evidence/fixed-menu-navigation-2026-10-04/slide-forward-960x540.png) shows one stationary top bar above sliding content. Previous whole-page motion screenshots above are historical.
+
+`DeployAndroid -QuickValidation` (`DeployAndroid-2264`) passes import/startup, driving 72, catalog 21 and menu presentation 48 checks, export, installation and cold launch on the attached DN2103 (803 ms). The same three existing driving shutdown instance warnings and build-tools fallback remain. Actual adb-generated left/right swipes were exercised on the final phone build; inspected [phone Garage transition](evidence/fixed-menu-navigation-2026-10-04/phone-garage-slide.png) shows the whole bar fixed while content/scenery move below it. A subsequent carousel-area swipe retains Race, which is left open for the owner. Phone finger feel, full Validate/replay, gameplay driving and thermal/performance acceptance remain untested. No backend/service action or mixed-tree commit. Changed files for this correction: `game/core/app.gd`, `game/tests/test_menu_page_swipe.gd`, this document, status/plan notes and the new evidence directory. A scoped cumulative menu patch and final verification/deployment logs are retained there; reverse-applicability and whitespace checks pass.
